diff --git a/tests/rust/purely_unsafe/manuallydrop_new_cfg/README.md b/tests/rust/purely_unsafe/manuallydrop_new_cfg/README.md
index 5a943905..f920c6c1 100644
--- a/tests/rust/purely_unsafe/manuallydrop_new_cfg/README.md
+++ b/tests/rust/purely_unsafe/manuallydrop_new_cfg/README.md
@@ -30,3 +30,22 @@ Expected result: exit status 1 with a dead-code diagnostic spanning the whole
 function. This is not a `req false` proof error. `mysh` does not express this
 expected exit status, so the fixture remains unregistered. Do not add
 `-allow_dead_code` or an assumption to make this case pass.
+
+## Expected-failure traversal
+
+`shared_false_unwind.rs` has a normal-first conditional after consuming `t`.
+The true branch reaches the common closing-brace return; the false branch calls
+`new(true)`, which really panics. VeriFast visits the translated true branch first.
+This records the shared normal return before the expected false unwind post aborts
+that function's verification. The previous unconditional fixture aborted before
+visiting this return and the separate mandatory dead-code pass then rejected the
+closing brace. No dead-code exemption or weaker unwind postcondition is used.
+`normal_first_cleanup` in the positive file has the same conditional and truthful
+thread-token posts. Cloud must confirm both real outcomes and the negative's
+exact post failure; an unused should_fail marker still rejects a missing unwind.
+
+The conditional is a tail expression: the `new(true)` arm has no semicolon.
+Its call result flows directly to the common return instead of adding an
+else-only goto after the call. Such a goto would remain unvisited when the
+expected unwind error ends this verification scope. The positive mirror has
+exactly the same tail-expression shape; Cloud must inspect the actual MIR/AST.
